Polly spend for the /design explainer — measured at the meter, 2026-09-16
========================================================================

WHY THIS RAN
  Two published numbers for the same quantity were both wrong. First '≈ $1.8',
  arithmetic on a remembered character count. Then '$0.121', derived from
  'video/out/audio/ holds exactly 20 mp3s, one per scene per language, so
  nothing was billed twice'. That derivation is INVALID: render.py --verify
  does 'shutil.rmtree(OUT / "audio")' between the two renders (render.py:306,
  comment '# force a second synthesis'), so the cache is deliberately destroyed
  mid-run and its final contents are one pass's worth no matter how many
  passes were billed. A local artifact cannot bound a spend that a remote
  meter records.

