COST EXPLORER — why today reads $0 and that is a LAG, not a zero
  2026-08-01 -> 2026-09-01  final
    USE1-SynthesizeSpeechGenerative-Characters       11060 ch  $0.331800  ($30.00/M)
    USE1-SynthesizeSpeechNeural-Characters            8971 ch  $0.143536  ($16.00/M)
  2026-09-01 -> 2026-09-16  ESTIMATED
    (no groups — the same filter returns two groups for August, so the
     filter is right and September is simply not processed yet)

STANDING RULE THIS ESTABLISHES
  Spend is read from the meter (CloudWatch RequestCharacters now, Cost Explorer
  after its lag), never inferred from a local artifact. And a $0 from Cost
  Explorer is a claim about the query, not about the account.
